    "text": "To determine how much money Tyrone has, we need to calculate the value of each type of currency he found and then sum these values.\n\n1. **Calculate the value of the $1 bills:**\n   Tyrone has 2 $1 bills.\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 1 = 2 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the value of the $5 bill:**\n   Tyrone has 1 $5 bill.\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 5 = 5 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the value of the quarters:**\n   Each quarter is worth $0.25. Tyrone has 13 quarters.\n   \\[\n   13 \\times 0.25 = 3.25 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the value of the dimes:**\n   Each dime is worth $0.10. Tyrone has 20 dimes.\n   \\[\n   20 \\times 0.10 = 2 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the value of the nickels:**\n   Each nickel is worth $0.05. Tyrone has 8 nickels.\n   \\[\n   8 \\times 0.05 = 0.40 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the value of the pennies:**\n   Each penny is worth $0.01. Tyrone has 35 pennies.\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 0.01 = 0.35 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nNow, we sum the values of all the currencies:\n\\[\n2 + 5 + 3.25 + 2 + 0.40 + 0.35 = 12.00 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total amount of money Tyrone has is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
